window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":901,"title":"Chapter 901: 902. One Brooch, I Concede.","paragraphs":["The first day of the Lunar New Year.","Weibo’s hot searches exploded.","#A Million-Yuan Lucky Bag Has Been Won# — Trending!","#Elderly Man from the Mountains Wins One Million# — Trending!","#Has ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍WeTalk Crashed?# — Boiling!","#I Shook for Three Minutes and Only Got Sixty-Eight Cents# — Boiling!","#Longfutong Linked More Than Fifty-Three Million Bank Cards# — Hot!","An official Weibo announcement confirmed that, in a remote mountain village in BS Province, an elderly man had won a million-yuan lucky bag. For privacy reasons, however, his identity had not been disclosed.","The moment the news came out, the comments section erupted.","“Holy crap! One million! An actual million yuan in cash!”","“That old man from the mountains became a millionaire with one casual shake, while I shook for ten minutes and only got five yuan and twenty cents. Is this what they call fate?”","“Be grateful for your five yuan. I only got three. I feel like WeTalk is psychologically manipulating me.”","“You’re all focused on the wrong thing. The real point is Longfutong. How long has it been? Its number of linked bank cards has already shot past fifty-three million. Do you know what that means? It took Taobao seven or eight years to build up its payment users, and Longfutong nearly caught up overnight.”","“Taobao: Is there no justice left in this world? I’ve spent seven or eight years building a payment platform, and they caught up in one night.”","“Looks like Ma Yunyun won’t be getting any sleep tonight.”","“Ma Yunyun: Why am I the one getting splashed when you two are fighting?”","“Seriously, don’t you find this terrifying? WeTalk launched a red-packet campaign and actually tied the two Mas together before pinning them to the ground. That’s absolutely brutal!”","“......”","Hangzhou. Taobao headquarters.","The New Year duty roster was normally divided into shifts. In previous years, only about half the employees would have been working at this time.","But this year, not a single person in the payments department had taken leave. Everyone was in the office.","Even Ma Yunyun himself had come in and was personally watching the real-time data on the giant screen.","Two curves were engaged in a fierce chase.","The blue line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to their payment platform. After seven or eight years, that number had accumulated to more than eighty million.","The red line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to Longfutong.","Before New Year’s Eve, the red curve had stood at only one-tenth of the blue one.","But from the period before New Year’s Eve onward, the red line began climbing at an almost vertical angle, as if it had been injected with stimulants.","Ten million. Twenty million. Thirty million...","It kept surging until it passed fifty million.","Today, the red line officially broke through the sixty-million mark, leaving it only a little more than twenty million behind the blue line.","“We’ve been doing this for seven or eight years.”","“They caught up in a single Spring Festival.”","Ma Yunyun watched as the members of the payments team sat in silence, their expressions complicated. But he did not blame them.","“I don’t blame any of you.”","“Wanlong Group’s Spring Festival Gala red-packet campaign was indeed an ingenious move. It caught us completely off guard, and it’s absolutely worth studying and reflecting on.”","“President Ma, could we launch a similar campaign?” the head of the marketing department asked.","Ma Yunyun shook his head. “We could, but it would have to wait until next Spring Festival. Doing it now wouldn’t mean anything. They already control the pace.”","He paused, then suddenly let out a laugh. “I, Ma Yunyun, have worked in the internet industry for so many years, and this is the first time someone has beaten me so thoroughly that I couldn’t even fight back. That Liu Yutong really is a genius. I concede.”","Everyone present exchanged glances.","Who was Ma Yunyun?","He was the madman universally acknowledged by the internet industry. When he was running Alibaba, he had dared to go head-to-head with eBay. When he entered the payments industry, he had dared to challenge the banks.","The entire business world of Longguo probably couldn’t produce a second person who could make him say, “I concede.”","“Technical team, listen up.”","“Here!”","“Starting tomorrow, put all your effort into developing a red-packet function. The features must be comprehensive, the experience must be smooth, and the interface must be stable. We must be able to do everything WeTalk can do—and whatever WeTalk can’t do, we must find a way to do as well.”","“Yes!”","Ma Yunyun took one last look at the red line still shooting upward on the giant screen, then turned and left the war room.","In the corridor, he pulled out his phone and opened WeTalk. He stared at the blue-green globe icon for a long time.","Then he held down the icon and tapped Uninstall.","After uninstalling it, he stood there silently for ten seconds before downloading WeTalk again from the app store.","Forget it. He’d give Liu Yutong some face.","............","Shencheng. GooseChat headquarters.","The ashtray on Pony Ma’s desk was already stuffed with cigarette butts, and the air was thick with tobacco smoke.","Pony Ma normally didn’t smoke much, but today he had already gone through more than half a pack.","On the computer screen before him were the figures sent over by his subordinates.","On New Year’s Eve, GooseChat had barely managed to gain five million new users.","Under normal circumstances, that would have been an excellent result. But compared with WeTalk’s more than forty million new users, those five million looked completely insignificant.","And if they counted from when WeTalk began its Five Blessings collection campaign before New Year’s Eve, its growth was far more than forty million.","Looking at the number of new users, Pony Ma suddenly felt like laughing.","A little over a month ago, Liu Yutong had told him, “Within two months, WeTalk’s user base will exceed GooseChat’s by at least thirty million.”","At the time, he had thought that goal was impossible.","Now, only a month and a half had passed, and the gap had probably already exceeded the target by nearly twice that amount.","“President Ma.”","The secretary entered carrying a cup of hot tea. “You haven’t slept all night. Why don’t you get some rest?”","“No need. How far has the data been updated?”","“WeTalk has just released its latest figures. Its total number of registered users has surpassed 120 million.”","Pony Ma nodded. “Got it. You can leave.”","After the secretary left, he was once again alone in the office.","Pony Ma took out the dark-gold invitation to the Dark Phoenix Society and examined it for a long time. At last, he opened it and removed the letter and the token inside.","The letter itself was nothing special. It merely contained the invitation.","The important item was the token—a brooch.","The brooch was only about the size of a thumb, and its design was identical to the black phoenix on the letter: wings spread, head lowered, red eyes glaring.","He had no idea what material it was made of, but it felt surprisingly heavy in his hand.","Pony Ma stared at the brooch for a long time.","Finally, he picked up his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message.","It contained only five words.","I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.","............","The morning of the first day of the New Year.","When Liu Yutong received Pony Ma’s text, she was back in her hometown setting off fireworks with Yaya.","Yaya was wearing a red padded jacket and clutching a handful of sparklers. She hopped and bounced around in the open space. Even though fireworks were nowhere near as beautiful in the daytime as they were at night, she was still having the time of her life.","“Big Sister, what do you think the Nian beast looks like?” Yaya asked, turning around while waving her sparkler.","“Probably like a really, really big dog.”","“Then why is it afraid of firecrackers?”","“Because firecrackers are too loud. Its ears can’t stand them.”","“Oh...” Yaya suddenly understood. “So the Nian beast isn’t actually bad. Its ears are just bigger, so it’s more afraid of loud noises?”","Liu Yutong laughed.","“That’s right. The Nian beast isn’t bad. Its ears are just bigger, and it’s more sensitive to loud sounds.”","“Then I won’t call it the Nian beast anymore. I’ll call it Big Dog Whose Ears Hate Loud Noises.”","Yaya was very pleased with the new name she had chosen for herself. She raised the spent sparkler and began running around the courtyard again.","Watching her little figure dart back and forth, Liu Yutong couldn’t help reminding her, “Be careful. Don’t fall.”","Just then, the phone in her pocket vibrated.","She pulled it out and saw a text message on the screen.","It contained only a few simple words.","[I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.]","After reading the message, Liu Yutong calmly slipped the phone back into her pocket, then waved to Yaya.","“Yaya, come here. I’ll show you how to set off a big one.”","“What big one?”","Liu Yutong found a cylindrical firework inside the house and placed it on the stone slab in the middle of the courtyard. Then she crouched down and lit the fuse with a lighter.","The fuse hissed and burned as the sisters backed away several steps together.","Three seconds later, a silver burst of light shot from the firework and exploded into a huge golden flower.","Then came a second burst, followed by a third... Silver and red fireworks continued exploding in succession above the courtyard, creating a breathtaking display.","“Wow!”","“Big Sister, these fireworks are so beautiful! What are they called?”","“These are called ‘A Courtyard Full of Red.’”"]},{"number":902,"title":"Chapter 902: 903, Sign the Letter of Intent","paragraphs":["The second day of the Lunar New Year, in Mingzhu City.","When Pony Ma’s private car pulled up in front of Shunchang Tower, he glanced out the window and froze.","The entrance to Shunchang Tower was packed with people.","They were all dressed in identical black suits, each wearing the same silver dragon-shaped badge. From the entrance all the way to the roadside, they stood in two perfectly orderly rows—at least two or three hundred of them.","With that kind of spectacle and oppressive presence, anyone who didn’t know better might have thought a foreign head of state had come for a visit.","The corner of Pony Ma’s mouth twitched.","He couldn’t tell whether Liu Yutong had arranged such an elaborate welcome for him or was trying to give him a show of force.","Probably both.","“P-President Ma, we’re here,” the driver said cautiously.","Pony Ma took a deep breath and pushed open the door.","The moment he stepped out, the two rows of men in black turned their heads in perfect unison. Hundreds of eyes landed on him at once.","For one brief moment, Pony Ma seriously considered sitting right back down in the car.","Just then, there was movement by the entrance to Shunchang Tower.","Liu Yutong came out to greet him.","She was wearing another black suit today, with that distinctive solid-gold dragon-shaped badge pinned to her chest. Her long hair fell loosely over her shoulders, and a faint smile rested on her face.","Yun Cheng and Lan Die followed half a step behind her. Behind them was a group of core members wearing platinum-colored badges, every one of them carrying an extraordinary air.","“President Ma, Happy New Year,” Liu Yutong said as she approached and extended her hand.","Pony ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Ma hurried forward and took it. “Director Liu, Happy New Year. This reception of yours... I’m honestly overwhelmed by the honor.”","“President Ma is an esteemed guest. It’s only proper.” Liu Yutong smiled faintly and gestured toward the building. “Please, come inside.”","The two of them walked into Shunchang Tower side by side, followed by the rows of men in black.","As he walked, Pony Ma couldn’t help reflecting to himself.","He had been dealing with Liu Yutong for quite some time, but every meeting with her managed to shock him all over again.","The elevator rose all the way to the forty-eighth floor.","When the conference-room door opened, several people were already inside.","Zhang Dalong, head of WeChat and one of the central figures in the merger negotiations.","Zhao Tianyi, chief legal officer of the Wanlong Association Group, wearing his trademark gold-rimmed glasses.","The other two were the heads of legal and finance who had flown in ahead of time from Big Goose. They were both Pony Ma’s trusted aides, and at that moment they sat stiffly upright.","They hadn’t expected the Wanlong Association headquarters to be this intimidating. Everywhere they looked, there were men in black.","“President Ma, please take a seat.” Liu Yutong sat down at the head of the table.","Pony Ma took the seat opposite her. One glance at the documents on the table was enough for him to understand roughly what was coming.","“President Ma, what do you have to say about the bet we made before?” Liu Yutong asked.","Pony Ma gave a bitter laugh. “Director Liu, there’s nothing left to say. I concede. And I concede wholeheartedly.”","Even now, thinking about that bet made his face burn with embarrassment.","Two months earlier, Liu Yutong had told him that WeChat would surpass GooseChat by thirty million users within two months.","At the time, he had thought the woman must be out of her mind. GooseChat had the enormous traffic pool of QQ behind it. The difference between the two platforms was only a few million users. How could WeChat possibly open up a thirty-million-user lead in just two months?","And then what happened?","Liu Yutong threw ten billion yuan into a Spring Festival red-envelope campaign, and the entire country went crazy.","On New Year’s Eve, Pony Ma had watched with his own eyes as WeChat’s new-user curve shot upward at an almost vertical angle. There was no stopping it.","When he checked the results on the morning of the first day of the new year, WeChat’s registered users had soared to 120 million, while GooseChat was still hovering around sixty million.","What was even more outrageous was that the red-envelope campaign had also managed to knock Old Ma flat in the process.","LongPay’s number of users with linked bank cards had surged by tens of millions over the course of the holiday. The defensive moat that Taobao had spent seven or eight years building had nearly been blasted flat by a single Spring Festival campaign.","Honestly, Pony Ma even felt a little sorry for Old Ma.","The man had only wanted to watch the show from the sidelines. He hadn’t provoked anyone or done anything wrong.","“President Ma, you’re being too serious. Business competition is like that. Sometimes you win, sometimes you lose. It’s perfectly normal.” Liu Yutong turned and nodded at Zhao Tianyi. “Tianyi, let’s begin.”","Zhao Tianyi adjusted his gold-rimmed glasses, opened the thick stack of documents in front of him, cleared his throat, and began reading through the key clauses of the merger agreement one by one.","“Clause One: WeChat will retain independent brand operations, while GooseChat will be incorporated into WeChat.”","Pony Ma nodded slightly.","They had already reached a consensus on this point. Once WeChat was folded into Big Goose, there would be no reason to keep GooseChat. Otherwise, it would simply be a waste of resources.","“Clause Two: Mr. Zhang Dalong will continue to serve concurrently as president of the WeChat division and report to the board of directors of Big Goose Group. The WeChat team will retain an independent organizational structure, with its offices located in Mingzhu City.”","At this, Pony Ma couldn’t help giving Zhang Dalong a long, deep look.","He regretted more than ever letting this man leave back then. If Zhang Dalong were still at Goose Factory, how could any of this have happened? WeChat might have been his product by now.","Of course, he had no idea that Zhang Dalong had also been in an extremely difficult position at the time.","“Clause Three: The Wanlong Association Group will contribute all of WeChat’s assets, along with an additional cash investment, in exchange for a thirty-percent stake in Big Goose Group, thereby becoming its largest shareholder.”","Pony Ma’s eyelid twitched violently.","Thirty percent.","He understood better than anyone what that figure meant.","Big Goose’s ownership structure was already highly dispersed. Nanfei, the foreign corporation, held more than thirty percent. He and several members of the founding team held only a little over ten percent combined, while the rest consisted of scattered shares traded on the secondary market.","Now Liu Yutong was suddenly going to become the largest shareholder. That meant Nanfei would have to give way—or even be forced out entirely.","More importantly, who knew whether The Young Lady would go completely mad and continue buying up shares on the secondary market, increasing her stake step by step until she achieved outright control?","If that happened, he really would be finished.","But that was a problem for later. He had lost the bet, and when you lost, you had to accept it.","For now, all he could do was find a way to place restrictions in the agreement and prevent her from increasing her stake without limits.","Of course, it was still too early to discuss that.","“Director Liu, how do you intend to deal with Nanfei?”","That was exactly the question Liu Yutong had been waiting for.","“Since you’re here, President Ma, I’ll be direct. I’d like to ask you to personally invite the people from Nanfei to come to Mingzhu City.”","“Tell them you’re inviting them to watch the Longteng Cup final on the day of the Lantern Festival.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Invite them to watch a match?","Looking at the smile on her face, Pony Ma suddenly felt a chill run down his back. Surely this woman wasn’t planning to seize control by force?","“Director Liu, you’re not thinking of...”","“Don’t worry, President Ma. We’re a legitimate private enterprise. We never do anything illegal.”","“I merely want to give our foreign friend an up-close experience of the Wanlong Association’s corporate culture. That’s all.”","Corporate culture.","When those four words came from Liu Yutong’s mouth, Pony Ma found them unnerving no matter how he interpreted them.","He couldn’t help recalling the rumors about the Ten Thousand Dragons Society—stories about fleets of hundreds of identical luxury sedans, thousands of men in black surrounding powerful underworld figures, and people being forced to jump from buildings in front of the police...","Forget it. No point thinking about it.","The more he thought about it, the harder it would be to fall asleep.","Pony Ma finally agreed. “All right. I’ll contact him as soon as I get back and ask him to come over.”","It wasn’t as if he was the one playing the villain. He was only passing along a message.","Liu Yutong nodded. “Tianyi, continue.”","Zhao Tianyi pushed up his glasses and went on reading the remaining clauses.","“Clause Four: Mr. Ma will continue to serve as chairman and CEO of Big Goose Group, and his authority over the company’s day-to-day operations and management will not be interfered with.”","Pony Ma felt slightly relieved when he heard this.","At least on the surface, he would still be the captain of Big Goose. He would still have his hands on the wheel.","But before he could fully relax, Zhao Tianyi immediately read the next clause.","“Clause Five: Ms. Liu Yutong undertakes never to increase her shareholding. However, as the largest shareholder, she will have veto power over major strategic decisions.”","Pony Ma’s expression instantly became a sight to behold.","“You call that not interfering with day-to-day operations? You even want veto power!”","“I’m only making sure no one takes advantage of you. That’s called supervision,” Liu Yutong said matter-of-factly.","“What are you supervising?”","“Making sure you don’t make foolish decisions.”","Liu Yutong casually gave him a few examples. “For instance, how Big Goose nearly sold QQ for one million back then. Or how your company actually dared to pay employees in cryptocurrency. And the whole forced either-or fiasco... Haven’t you people made enough foolish decisions already?”","Pony Ma: “...”","He wanted to argue, but every one of those things had really happened.","Zhao Tianyi continued reading the clauses that followed.","There were anti-dilution protections, preemptive subscription rights, arrangements for board seats, and more. Each provision was laid out in meticulous detail, leaving no loopholes unaddressed.","The more Pony Ma listened, the more alarmed he became.","This agreement had taken every possible loophole into consideration. There was no way their legal team could have drafted something so comprehensive without preparing for several months.","In other words, Liu Yutong hadn’t set her sights on Big Goose on a whim. She had been plotting this for a long time.","After all the clauses had been read, Zhao Tianyi closed the document and said calmly, “If neither of you has any objections, you may sign.”","Pony Ma picked up the pen and paused for several seconds over the signature line.","Once he signed, Big Goose would change forever.","The empire he had founded and painstakingly managed for more than a decade would now have another, even more formidable major shareholder.","But in the end, he gritted his teeth and signed his name with a series of quick strokes.","Liu Yutong took the pen and signed her name as well.","The two exchanged the documents and signed them again.","Zhang Dalong, Zhao Tianyi, and the legal and financial representatives from Big Goose then signed in turn.","Of course, what they were signing for the moment was only a letter of intent. Nan Fei’s shares had yet to be acquired, and given the significance of the matter, everything had to remain confidential at this stage.","Only after the situation with Nan Fei had been completely settled would the agreement officially take effect.","Still, this marked a crucial first step.","From this day forward, it could be said that Liu Yutong had effectively taken control of most of Long Kingdom’s internet industry.","Liu Yutong stood and extended her hand toward Pony Ma. “President Ma, we’re family from now on.”","Pony Ma shook her hand, his smile somewhat strained. “Director Liu, I’ll be counting on your guidance from now on.”","“Of course.”","Liu Yutong released his hand, then suddenly thought of something.","“Oh, right, President Ma. When Nan Fei’s largest shareholder arrives, please come along and help receive him. After all, you’ve worked together for so many years. It would be more appropriate for you to be there.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Receive him? What kind of reception was this?","Why didn’t she receive the person she had invited herself? Why did she have to drag him into it?","A sudden, ominous feeling came over him.","Something major was bound to happen on the day of the Lantern Festival."]}]);
